# Shell scripts must always be LF in every checkout: they are invoked via
# POSIX sh (gate registries, hooks, CI), and a CRLF working copy breaks
# strict sh implementations (dash) even though Git Bash tolerates it.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending-normalised. Without this, Git's text
# auto-detection tried to CRLF→LF the committed screenshot PNGs on checkout,
# corrupting them and leaving them permanently "modified" in the working tree
# (which also blocked rebases). `binary` = `-text -diff`.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.eot  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
